{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Say to all the people of the land</b> — these are the people of Babylon and also the people of Jerusalem, for the prophecy includes everything, and also to the priests who do not know how to answer." "<b>And mourn</b> — a verb form; thus it is וספדתם ספוד, and behold [Isaiah] took a shortened path." "<b>On the fifth</b> — it is the one mentioned, and he added also the seventh that follows it, and it is the fast of Gedaliah. And he mentioned these seventy years; he did not scruple to mention two additional years or one, for in the second year of Darius the king the seventy years of Jerusalem's destruction were completed, and this prophecy was in the fourth year, and part of the third had already entered when the seventy were completed; and by this prophecy part of the fourth has already entered. Therefore he did not calculate precisely the count of seventy, for it is close." "<b>And the word 'fast'</b> — from the standing verbs [i.e., active participles functioning as nouns]." "<b>Therefore you fasted for me</b> — you fasted on my account or for my honor, for I did not command you to fast."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:17.136539846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}